  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Commerce obligated $5B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The department executed 9,470 awards with an average award size of $532K, and obligations were up 21.2% year over year. The FY2026 total equals the FY23 total at $5B and follows recent year totals of $4.2B in FY25 and $5.2B in FY24. The largest spending categories in FY2026 to date are Other Computer Related Services at $912M, Computer Systems Design Services at $660M, and Custom Computer Programming Services at $540M. The top vendors by obligations in FY2026 to date include REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC at $218M, PERATON INC. at $163M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $141M. The figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations; current-year totals are partial and will change as the fiscal year progresses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Where is Commerce spending its contract dollars?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce is concentrating spending in technology and professional services. Other Computer Related Services leads at $912M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $660M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $540M. The department also obligated funds to publishing, management consulting, ship building and research categories, including All Other Publishers at $220M and Ship Building and Repairing at $190M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who receives the largest Commerce awards?",
        "body": "The Department of Commerce’s largest vendors are concentrated in IT, defense, and professional services. REED TECHNOLOGY AND INFORMATION SERVICES LLC received $218M, PERATON INC. received $163M, and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $141M. The top ten vendor list also includes LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $136M and THE MITRE CORPORATION at $89.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
