    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Commerce spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Commerce obligated $5B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The department made 9,470 awards with an average award size of $532K and obligations were up 21.2% year over year. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent partial current-year totals."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Commerce buy?",
      "a": "Commerce buys primarily technology and professional services. Other Computer Related Services accounted for $912M, Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $660M, and Custom Computer Programming Services accounted for $540M. Commerce also bought publishing, consulting, ship building, and research services across other categories."
